**Read:** [Reproducible Research in Computational Science — Peng](../sources/Reproducibility-and-Replication.lingua#r_32SK41ZP8P04Z0PMZX5NN6C2T9), the complete article; [The Turing Way — reproducible research, collaboration, and preservation](../sources/The-Turing-Way.lingua#r_5K6W3KETGFH4N3SDYCB5V0Q3MZ), Overview, Definitions, and the linked reproducibility discussions.

Several useful claims are often hidden inside the word reproducible. State the one you actually test. A byte comparison asks whether two artifacts contain exactly the same bytes. Numerical reproduction asks whether specified quantities agree under a stated rule. Independent implementation asks whether another expression of the method yields the expected result. Scientific replication asks what happens with new observations or a new experiment. Terminology varies between communities; preserve the operational definition in a report.

A JSON file with a different timestamp fails a byte comparison even if its scientific quantities agree. Two programs can print identical numbers because both use the same erroneous formula. Conversely, two correctly implemented floating-point algorithms can differ in their last digits without changing a supported conclusion. These are different findings, each needing its own evidence.

For each project name inputs, method, environment, expected outputs, and comparison criterion. Decide whether row order, whitespace, metadata, rounding, or a stochastic interval belongs in that criterion. Explain the scale of numerical tolerance in the units and use of the result. Choose it before seeing a disappointing discrepancy.

**Work:** define acceptance for the two-lot calculation at three levels: identical input/code bytes producing identical report bytes; reordered input rows producing the same scientific totals; an independent spreadsheet obtaining the same exact fractions. Explain why the first claim should include input identity while the second intentionally changes it. Later add an uncertain-input simulation and specify a statistical comparison instead of demanding equal sample means from different random streams.

Preserve failures as evidence about the claim's limits. “It ran on my machine” establishes one execution under partly observed conditions. A reconstruction experiment changes that evidence only when the other inputs, environment, procedure, and comparison are actually inspected.

